===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[confusing]], disorganized [[situation]] often attributed to or marked by human error.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010 |title=Talking to Terrorists: Why America Must Engage with Its Enemies|author=Mark Perry |page= |ISBN=|passage=Never did find out what happened in July, but that was a '''goat rope''' that was poorly coordinated.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013 |title=Due Process|author=Lyle O’Connor |page= |ISBN=|passage=What a '''goat rope'''! The fact that we had to appear three different times was certainly an indicator things were going poorly for the prosecution.}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[convoluted]] [[issue]] that is [[contest]]ed by many parties.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013 |title=Surviving Home|author=A. American |page= 32|ISBN=|passage=“How far up does this little '''goat rope''' go?” Sarge asked. “As far as we know, all the way to the commander in chief.”}}
# A [[rodeo]] event in which competitors attempt to [[lasso]] a goat, usually for younger participants.
# An ill-advised solution to contain a problem; a solution that will eventually fail.

